---
pre-compare: sort
---

// Synthetic PAN-OS Correlated Events record; every value is invented. The
// column order follows the PAN-OS 11.1 Correlated Events log fields.
// https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/administration/monitoring/use-syslog-for-monitoring/syslog-field-descriptions/correlated-events-log-fields
// The correlation object becomes the analytic and the evidence text the
// finding description. The record has no sequence number, so the required
// finding UID stays missing.
from_file env("TENZIR_INPUT") {
  read_lines
}
this = line.parse_syslog()
paloalto::ocsf::normalize
this = ocsf_cast(ocsf_derive(this))
drop raw_data, raw_data_size
drop_null_fields
